hadiths[128]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3084","[AI-translation] From Ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Jibril came to me wearing green, with pearls suspended from it."
"3085","[AI-translation] From Hakim bin Hizam, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) was among his companions, he said to them: Do you hear what I hear? They said: We do not hear anything. He said: I hear the creaking of the heaven, and it is not to be blamed for creaking, and there is no spot in it the size of a hand-span except that upon it is an angel prostrating or standing."
"3086","On the authority of Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""I was brought the Burāq, and it is a white beast, long, that places its hoof at the farthest point of its sight. So we did not cease from its back—I and Jibrīl, peace be upon him—until we came to Bayt al-Maqdis. Then the gates of heaven were opened for us, and I saw Paradise and Hell."" Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān said: ""And he did not pray in Bayt al-Maqdis."" Zirr said: ""So I said to him: 'Rather, he did pray.'"" Ḥudhayfah said: ""What is your name, O bald one! For I recognize your face but I do not know your name?"" I said: ""I am Zirr ibn Ḥubaysh."" He said: ""And how do you know that he prayed?"" I said: ""Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: {Glory be to Him who took His servant by night from the Sacred Mosque to the Farthest Mosque whose surroundings We have blessed, to show him of Our signs. Indeed He is the Hearing, the Seeing} (17:1)."" He said: ""So do you find in it that he prayed? If he had prayed, you would have prayed in it just as you pray in the Sacred Mosque."" Zirr said: ""And he tied the beast to the ring to which the prophets, peace be upon them, tie."" Ḥudhayfah said: ""Or was he afraid it would go away from him when Allah had brought it to him?"""
"3087","[AI-translation] From Anas, from Jundub or someone else among the Companions, from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) who said: Adam and Musa argued, and Adam out-argued Musa."
"3088","[AI-translation] Harith ibn Hisham asked the Prophet, peace be upon him: How does the revelation come to you? He said: Sometimes it comes to me like the ringing of a bell, and that is the hardest on me, then it departs from me and I have retained it. And sometimes the angel comes to me in the likeness of a man, and I understand what he says."
"3089","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, he said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, took the covenant from the back of Adam at Na'man, meaning Arafah. He brought forth from his loins all the descendants He had created and scattered them before him like ants. Then He addressed them face to face, saying: ""Am I not your Lord?"" They said: ""Yes, we have witnessed."" Lest you should say on the Day of Resurrection, ""Indeed, we were of this unaware."" (172) Or lest you say, ""It was only that our fathers associated others in worship with Allah before, and we were but descendants after them. So would You destroy us for what the falsifiers did?"" (173) Al-A'raf."
"3090","[AI-translation] From Jabir, raised to the Prophet: I have been given permission to speak about an angel from the angels of Allah, Exalted be He, among the bearers of the Throne: the distance between his earlobe and his shoulder is a journey of seven hundred years."
"3091","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, and said: O Muhammad! ""And a Garden whose width is that of the heavens and the earth"" (Aal Imran: 133), so where is the Fire? He said: ""Have you seen this night that has covered everything for you, where is it placed?"" He said: Allah knows best. He said: ""Indeed Allah does whatever He wills."
"3092","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: The Fire complained to its Lord and said: ""Parts of me are consuming other parts."" So He made for it two breaths: a breath in winter and a breath in summer. As for its breath in winter, it is the bitter cold, and as for its breath in summer, it is the scorching wind."
"3093","[AI-translation] From Ubaydullah ibn Anas (mursal): The most wretched of the former peoples is the one who hamstrung the she-camel, and the most wretched of the latter peoples is the one who will stab you, O Ali. And he gestured to where he would stab him."
"3094","On the authority of Abu Musa, who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he honored him. He said to him: ""Come to us."" So he came to him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said — and in another narration: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) alighted with a Bedouin and honored him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""Fulfill our covenant, come to us."" So the Bedouin came to him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""Ask for your need."" He said: ""A camel with its saddle, and goats that my family can milk."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Are you incapable of being like the old woman of the Children of Israel?"" (His companions said: ""O Messenger of Allah! And what is the old woman of the Children of Israel?"") He said: ""When Musa traveled with the Children of Israel from Egypt, they lost the way. He said: 'What is this?' Their scholars said: 'We will inform you: When death approached Yusuf, he took a covenant from us by Allah that we would not leave Egypt until we carry his bones with us.' He said: 'Who knows the location of his grave?' (They said: 'We do not know where Yusuf's grave is, except') an old woman from the Children of Israel. He sent for her, and she came to him. He said: 'Guide me to Yusuf's grave.' She said: 'No, by Allah, I will not do so until you give me my judgment.' He said: 'And what is your judgment?' She said: 'That I be with you in Paradise.' He disliked giving her that. Then Allah revealed to him: 'Give her her judgment.' So she went with them to a lake, a place where water collected. She said: 'Drain this water.' So they drained it. She said: 'Dig and bring out Yusuf's bones.' When they brought them up to the surface, behold, the path became like the light of day."""
"3095","[AI-translation] From Anas, raised to the Prophet: Yusuf, peace be upon him, was given half of all beauty."
"3096","[AI-translation] From Awf ibn Malik, raised to the Prophet: The Jews split into seventy-one sects; one is in Paradise and seventy are in the Fire. And the Christians split into seventy-two sects; one is in Paradise and seventy-one are in the Fire. And by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, my nation will split into seventy-three sects; one is in Paradise and seventy-two are in the Fire. It was said: O Messenger of Allah! Who are they? He said: The community (al-Jama'ah)."
"3097","[AI-translation] From Mujahid he said: We were with Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, and they mentioned the Dajjal. He said: It is written between his eyes: Kafir. He said: Ibn Abbas said: I did not hear it. He said: That is so, but he said: ""As for Ibrahim, look at your companion. And as for Musa, he is a dark-skinned man with curly hair upon a red camel haltered with a fiber rope, as if I am looking at him as he descends into the valley reciting the Talbiyah."
"3098","[AI-translation] From Abu Dharr, raised to the Prophet: Indeed, Adam was created from three types of earth: black, white, and green."
"3099","[AI-translation] Rahman ibn Hasanah, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, on a journey, and we caught some dhab (lizards). The pots were boiling, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, said: ""A nation from the Children of Israel was transformed, and I fear that these may be them, meaning the dhab."" He said: So we overturned them while we were hungry."
"3100","[AI-translation] Fakah ibn al-Mughirah: That she entered upon 'A'ishah and saw a spear placed in her house. She said: ""O Mother of the Believers! What do you do with this spear?"" She said: ""We kill with it the geckos, for the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, informed us: that Ibrahim, peace be upon him, when he was cast into the fire, there was no creature except that it extinguished it for him except the gecko, for it was blowing on it."" So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, ordered its killing."
"3101","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah: Allah has permitted me to speak about a rooster whose legs have pierced the earth, and its neck is folded beneath the Throne, and it says: ""Glory be to You, how great You are, our Lord!"" So He replied to it: ""The one who swears by Me falsely does not know that."
"3102","[AI-translation] From Abu Nadhrah, he said: A man from the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, fell ill, so his companions entered upon him to visit him, and he wept. It was said to him: ""What makes you weep, O servant of Allah? Did not the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say to you: 'Trim your moustache, then let it be until you meet me?'"" He said: ""Yes, but I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, say: 'Allah, Blessed and Exalted, took a handful with His right hand and said: ""These are for these, and I do not care,"" and He took another handful,' meaning with His other hand, 'and said: ""These are for these, and I do not care."" So I do not know in which of the two handfuls I am.'"
"3103","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, he said: When Allah created the creation, He wrote with His hand upon Himself: ""Indeed, My mercy overcomes My anger."
"3104","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet: Indeed, Allah created Adam in His image, and his height was sixty cubits."
"3105","[AI-translation] Ash'ari, raised to the Prophet: Indeed, Allah created Adam from a handful that He took from all of the earth. So the children of Adam came according to the measure of the earth; from them came the red, the white, the black, and what is between that, the smooth, the rugged, the evil, and the good."
"3106","[AI-translation] 'As, raised to the Prophet: Indeed, Allah created His creation in darkness, then He cast upon them from His light. So whoever is touched by that light is guided, and whoever misses it goes astray. 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr said: Therefore I say: The pen has dried upon what is to be."
"3107","[AI-translation] Rahman ibn Qatadah al-Sulami, raised to the Prophet: Indeed, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, created Adam, then He took the creation from his back and said: ""These are to Paradise, and I do not care, and these are to the Fire, and I do not care."" So a speaker said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Then on what do we work?"" He said: ""Upon the places of destiny."
"3108","[AI-translation] From Anas, raised to the Prophet: ""Indeed, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, took a handful and said: 'In Paradise by My mercy,' and He took a handful and said: 'In the Fire, and I do not care.'"
"3109","Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd informed me; my father said: I was sitting next to Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān in the mosque when a handsome elderly man from Banū Ghifār passed by, and in his ears was deafness—or he said: heaviness (difficulty hearing). So Ḥumayd sent for him, and when he approached, he said: ""O son of my brother! Make room for him between me and you, for he accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."" So he came and sat between me and him. Ḥumayd said to him: ""Is this the ḥadīth that you narrated to me about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?"" The elderly man said: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, creates the clouds, so they speak the best of speech and laugh the best of laughter.'"""
"3110","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas, raised [to the Prophet]: ""Indeed, the first thing Allah Almighty created was the Pen, and He commanded it to write everything that will be."
"3111","[AI-translation] From Abdullah bin Mas'ud from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, he said: ""Indeed, the first to set free the Sa'ibah and worship the idols was Abu Khuzahah Amr bin 'Amir, and I saw him dragging his intestines in the Fire."
"3112","On the authority of ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: ""The Children of Israel appointed a caliph over them after Mūsā, peace be upon him. He stood praying one night above Bayt al-Maqdis in the moonlight, and mentioned certain deeds he had done. Then he descended by a rope. In the morning the rope was found hanging in the mosque, but he was gone. He went on until he came to a people on the seashore, and found them striking bricks or making bricks. He asked them: 'How do you bind this brick?' They informed him, so he made bricks with them. He would eat from the work of his hand. When the time for prayer came, he stood to pray. The workers reported this to their overseer: 'There is a man among us who does such and such.' He sent for him, but he refused to come to him three times. Then he came riding his mount. When the man saw him, he fled. The overseer followed him, but the man outran him. He said: 'Wait for me, let me speak to you.' So he stopped until he spoke to him, and informed him of his story—that he had been a king, and that he had fled out of awe of his Lord. The overseer said: 'I think I shall catch up with you.' So he followed him, and they both worshipped Allah until they died at Rumayla in Egypt."" ʿAbdullāh said: ""Had I been there, I would have been guided to their graves by the description the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us."""
"3113","[AI-translation] Ash'ari), raised [to the Prophet]: ""The Children of Israel wrote a book and followed it, and they abandoned the Torah."
"3114","On the authority of Rabi'ah ibn 'Amilah, who said: Abdullah narrated to us: ""We have not heard a hadith more beautiful than this except the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and a narration from the Prophet ﷺ. He said: 'When the time grew long for the Children of Israel and their hearts hardened, they fabricated a book from themselves. Their hearts were enamored of it, and their tongues made it lawful. The truth stood between them and many of their desires until they cast the Book of Allah behind their backs as if they did not know. They said: ""Present this book to the Children of Israel. If they follow you in it, leave them; and if they oppose you, kill them."" He said: ""No, rather send for so-and-so—a man from their scholars. If he follows you, no one will differ with you after him."" So they sent for him, called him, and he took a parchment, wrote in it the Book of Allah, then placed it in a horn, hung it around his neck, put his clothes over it, and came to them. They presented the book to him and said: ""Do you believe in this?"" He pointed to his chest—meaning the book that was in the horn—and said: ""I believe in this, and why should I not believe in this?"" So they let him go. He had companions who visited him. When death approached him, they came to him. When they removed his clothes, they found the horn in his chest containing the Book. They said: ""Do you not see his statement: 'I believe in this, and why should I not believe in this?' He meant by 'this' this Book that is in the horn."" He said: ""So the Children of Israel split into seventy-two sects, the best of their communities being the companions of the Father of the Horn."""
"3115","On the authority of Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""There were three men among the Children of Israel: a leper, a bald man, and a blind man. Allah wished to test them, so He sent an angel to them.The angel came to the leper and said: 'What thing is most beloved to you?' He said: 'A good complexion and good skin, and that which has caused people to shun me may depart from me.' The angel wiped him, and his impurity departed, and he was given a good complexion and good skin. The angel said: 'What wealth is most beloved to you?' He said: 'Camels' — or he said 'cattle,' Ishaq was uncertain, except that the leper or the bald man, one of them said: 'Camels,' and the other said: 'Cattle.' The angel said: 'You shall have a pregnant she-camel.' He said: 'May Allah bless it for you.'Then the angel came to the bald man and said: 'What thing is most beloved to you?' He said: 'Good hair, and that which has caused people to shun me may depart from me.' The angel wiped him, and it departed, and he was given good hair. The angel said: 'What wealth is most beloved to you?' He said: 'Cattle.' He was given a pregnant cow. The angel said: 'May Allah bless it for you.'Then the angel came to the blind man and said: 'What thing is most beloved to you?' He said: 'That Allah restore my sight so that I may see people.' The angel wiped him, and Allah restored his sight. The angel said: 'What wealth is most beloved to you?' He said: 'Sheep.' He was given a pregnant ewe.Then these two produced offspring, and this one produced offspring, so that one of them had a valley full of camels, another a valley full of cattle, and the third a valley full of sheep.Then the angel came to the leper in his form and appearance and said: 'A poor man, whose means have been exhausted in his journey, so that I have no way to reach my destination today except by Allah, then by you. I ask you by Him Who gave you the good complexion and good skin and wealth, for a camel to carry me on my journey.' He said: 'Rights are many.' The angel said: 'It is as if I know you. Were you not a leper whom people shunned, and poor? Then Allah gave you.' He said: 'I only inherited this wealth, generation after generation.' The angel said: 'If you are lying, may Allah return you to what you were.'Then the angel came to the bald man in his form and said to him the like of what he said to the first, and he replied with the like of what the first replied. The angel said: 'If you are lying, may Allah return you to what you were.'Then the angel came to the blind man in his form and appearance and said: 'A poor man and a wayfarer, whose means have been exhausted in his journey, so that I have no way to reach my destination today except by Allah, then by you. I ask you by Him Who restored your sight, for a sheep to sustain me on my journey.' He said: 'I was blind, and Allah restored my sight. Take what you wish and leave what you wish. By Allah, I will not make things difficult for you today for anything you take for the sake of Allah.' The angel said: 'Keep your wealth, for you were only tested. Allah is pleased with you and angry with your two companions.'"""
"3116","[AI-translation] From Ubayy bin Ka'b from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, that when Jibril struck Zamzam with his heel, the mother of Isma'il began to gather the sand. The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""May Allah have mercy on Hajar, the mother of Isma'il; had she left it, it would have been a flowing spring."
"3117","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""A man from the Children of Israel asked another man to lend him one thousand dinars. The lender said: 'Bring me witnesses to testify to this.' The borrower said: 'Allah is sufficient as a Witness.' The lender said: 'Then bring me a guarantor.' The borrower said: 'Allah is sufficient as a Guarantor.' The lender said: 'You have spoken the truth,' and he handed over one thousand dinars to him for a specified term.The borrower went out to sea and fulfilled his need. When the appointed term arrived, he sought a vessel to return the money but could not find one. He took a piece of wood, bored a hole in it, placed the one thousand dinars inside along with a note to its owner, sealed the spot, and brought it to the sea. He said: 'O Allah, You know that I borrowed one thousand dinars from so-and-so. He asked me for witnesses and I said: Allah is sufficient as a Witness. He asked me for a guarantor and I said: Allah is sufficient as a Guarantor. He accepted You. I strove to find a vessel to send him his due but could not find one, so I entrust this to You.' Then he threw it into the sea.The lender went out looking to see if a vessel might arrive with his money. He found the piece of wood containing the money, so he took it as firewood. When he broke it open, he found the money and the note. Later, the borrower arrived and said: 'By Allah, I could not find a vessel to set out on.' The lender said: 'Allah has delivered on your behalf what you sent in the piece of wood.' So the borrower departed with his one thousand dinars, rightly guided."""
"3118","On the authority of Abū Hurayrah, marfūʿan: Verily, the sun was never held back for any human being except for Yūshaʿ (Joshua) during the nights he marched toward Bayt al-Maqdis (Jerusalem). (And in a narration: A prophet from among the prophets went on a military expedition and said to his people: ""No man should follow me who has married a woman and wishes to consummate the marriage but has not yet done so; nor another who has built a building but has not yet raised its roof; nor another who has bought sheep or pregnant camels and is awaiting their offspring."") He said: So he went on the expedition and approached the village at the time of the ʿAṣr prayer or close to that. (And in a narration: He encountered the enemy at the setting of the sun.) He said to the sun: ""You are commanded and I am commanded. O Allah, hold it back for me a while."" So it was held back for him until Allah granted him victory. (So they collected the spoils.) He said: They gathered what they had won as spoils, and the fire came to consume it but refused to eat it. (And they used to be, when they won spoils, Allah would send fire upon it to eat it.) He said: ""There is ghulūl (stealing from spoils) among you. Let a man from each tribe pledge allegiance to me."" They pledged allegiance, and the hand of a man stuck to his hand. He said: ""The ghulūl is among you. Let your tribe pledge allegiance to me."" His tribe pledged allegiance, and the hands of two or three men stuck to his hand. He said: ""The ghulūl is among you; you have stolen."" (They said: ""Yes, we have stolen a golden cow's head."") He said: ""Bring it out to me."" They brought out something like a cow's head of gold. He said: He placed it among the spoils, and it was on the plain. The fire came and ate it. Spoils were not lawful for anyone before us, because Allah, Blessed and Exalted, saw our weakness and inability, so He made them lawful for us. (And in a narration: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said at that: ""Verily, Allah has made spoils lawful for us as a mercy to us and a lightening of what He knew of our weakness."")"
"3119","[AI-translation] From Abu Sa'id, that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""Indeed, Satan said: 'By Your Might, O Lord, I will not cease to misguide Your servants as long as their souls are in their bodies.' The Lord, Blessed and Exalted, said: 'By My Might and My Majesty, I will not cease to forgive them as long as they seek My forgiveness.'"
"3120","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, he said: ""Indeed, Satan has despaired of being worshipped in this land of yours, but he is satisfied with what you deem insignificant."
"3121","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""Indeed, Satan walks in a single sandal."
"3122","[AI-translation] From Abu Umamah, raised [to the Prophet]: ""Indeed, the companion on the left raises the pen for six hours from the Muslim servant who errs or commits a sin. If he regrets and seeks forgiveness from Allah, he casts it away; otherwise, he writes one."
"3123","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""The glance of the bearer of the Horn, since he was entrusted with it, is set, looking towards the Throne in fear that he may be commanded before his glance returns to him; his eyes are like two brilliant stars."
"3124","On the authority of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: ""I will not narrate to you except what I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; my ears heard it and my heart retained it. Verily, a man killed ninety-nine people, then the desire for repentance came to him. He asked about the most knowledgeable person on earth, and was directed to a man (and in a narration: a monk). He came to him and said: 'I have killed ninety-nine people; is there any repentance for me?' He said: 'After killing ninety-nine people?' So the man drew his sword and killed him, thereby completing one hundred.Then the desire for repentance came to him again. He asked about the most knowledgeable person on earth, and was directed to a man (a scholar). He came to him and said: 'I have killed one hundred people; is there any repentance for me?' He said: 'Who stands between you and repentance? Depart from the wicked village you are in to the good village, the village of such-and-such (for therein are people who worship Allah), and worship your Lord (with them) therein, and do not return to your land, for it is a land of evil.' So he set out for the good village, but death overtook him on the way (in the middle of the road) (and he leaned with his chest towards it).The angels of mercy and the angels of punishment disputed over him. Iblis said: 'I have more right to him, for he never disobeyed me for a single moment.' The angels of mercy said: 'He came out repenting (turning with his heart towards Allah),' and the angels of punishment said: 'He never did any good deed at all.' So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent an angel to them (in the form of a human) to arbitrate between them. He said: 'Measure the distance between the two villages; whichever he is closer to, he belongs to its people.' (So Allah revealed to this one: 'Draw near,' and Allah revealed to that one: 'Recede.') They measured him and found him closer to the land he intended by a cubit (or: by a span), so the angels of mercy took him (and he was forgiven).Al-Hasan said: 'When he realized death was near, he struggled with himself (and in a narration: he leaned with his chest towards it), so Allah, Mighty and Majestic, brought the good village near to him and distanced the wicked village from him, and they counted him among the people of the good village.'"""
"3125","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, stopped [at the companion]: ""Indeed, Pharaoh pegged his wife with four pegs in her hands and feet. When they dispersed from her, the angels shaded her. She said: 'My Lord, build for me near You a house in Paradise and save me from Pharaoh and his deed and save me from the wrongdoing people.' So He uncovered her house in Paradise to her."
"3126","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""The noble, son of the noble, son of the noble, son of the noble is Yusuf ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, the intimate friend of the Most Merciful, Blessed and Exalted be He. Had I remained in prison as long as Yusuf remained, and then the caller came to me, I would have responded. When the messenger came to him, he said: 'Ask him about the women who cut their hands' (Yusuf: 50). And may Allah have mercy on Lut; indeed he used to take refuge in a strong support when he said to his people: 'If only I had strength against you or could take refuge in a strong support' (Hud: 80). So Allah did not send any prophet after him except from the nobility of his people."""
"3127","On the authority of Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from his father, that Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq, ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, and a number of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat together after the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and discussed the gravest of major sins. They had no knowledge concerning it, so they sent me to ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ to ask him about it. He informed me that the gravest of major sins is drinking wine. I came to them and informed them, whereupon they denied it and all rushed toward him until they reached his house. He told them that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""A king from the Children of Israel seized a man and gave him the choice between drinking wine, killing a youth, committing adultery, eating pork, or being killed if he refused. He chose to drink the wine. When he drank it, he did not refuse them anything they wanted from him."" And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us at that time: ""No one drinks it and has his prayer accepted for forty nights, and no one dies while any of it remains in his bladder but that Paradise is forbidden to him. And if he dies within the forty days, he dies a death of ignorance (jāhiliyyah)."""
"3128","On the authority of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Moses said: 'O my Lord, show me Adam who caused us and himself to be expelled from Paradise.' So Allah showed him Adam. He said: 'Are you our father Adam?' Adam said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Are you the one into whom Allah breathed of His spirit, and taught you all the names, and commanded the angels to prostrate to you, so they prostrated?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then what caused you to expel us and yourself from Paradise?' Adam said to him: 'And who are you?' He said: 'I am Moses.' He said: 'Are you the prophet of the Children of Israel to whom Allah spoke from behind a veil, without placing between you and Him any messenger from His creation?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Did you not find that this was written in Allah's Book before I was created?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then why do you blame me for something that Allah had decreed before me?' The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said at that: 'So Adam got the better of Moses in argument, Adam got the better of Moses in argument.'"""
"3129","On the authority of Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), attributed to the Prophet (ﷺ): ""Indeed, Allah's Prophet Ayyub remained afflicted with his trial for eighteen years. Both near and far abandoned him, except two men from his brethren who would visit him morning and evening. One day, one of them said to his companion: 'Do you know, by Allah, Ayyub has committed a sin such as no one in the worlds has committed?' His companion asked: 'What is that?' He replied: 'For eighteen years, Allah has not shown him mercy so as to remove what afflicts him.' When they went to Ayyub, the man could not contain himself until he mentioned this to him. Ayyub said: 'I do not know what you two say, except that Allah knows that I used to pass by two men disputing, and they would mention Allah, so I would return to my house and make expiation for them, disliking that Allah be mentioned except in truth.'He would go out to relieve himself, and when he finished, his wife would hold his hand until he reached home. One day, he was delayed in returning to her, and Allah revealed to Ayyub: 'Strike the ground with your foot: this is a cool bath and drink' (Qur'an 38:42). She found him slow in returning, so she went out to meet him, looking on, and he was coming toward her, Allah having removed from him the affliction, and he was in the best state he had ever been. When she saw him, she said: 'May Allah bless you! Have you seen Allah's Prophet, this afflicted man? By Allah, upon that, I have not seen a man more resembling him than you, when he was healthy.' He said: 'Indeed, I am he.'He had two threshing floors (i.e., two threshing floors): one for wheat and one for barley. Allah sent two clouds. When one of them was over the wheat threshing floor, it poured gold into it until it overflowed, and the other poured silver into the barley threshing floor until it overflowed."""
"3130","Abdullah ibn Amr reported: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) when a man from the desert Arabs came wearing a coarse woolen cloak trimmed with silk brocade. He said: ""Behold, your companion here has put down every horseman son of a horseman""—meaning he wants to put down every horseman son of a horseman and raise every shepherd son of a shepherd. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) took hold of the collar of his cloak and said: ""Do I not see on you the clothing of one who does not understand?"" Then he said: ""Indeed, the Prophet of Allah Noah (peace be upon him), when death approached him, said to his son: 'I am relating to you the will: I command you with two things and forbid you from two things. I command you with ""There is no god but Allah""—for if the seven heavens and the seven earths were placed in one scale and ""There is no god but Allah"" was placed in the other, ""There is no god but Allah"" would outweigh them. And if the seven heavens and the seven earths were a sealed ring, ""There is no god but Allah"" would break them. And ""Glory be to Allah and with His praise""—for it is the prayer of everything, and by it the creation is provided for.' And I forbid you from shirk (associating partners with Allah) and kibr (arrogance)."" He said: I said—or it was said: ""O Messenger of Allah! This shirk we have recognized, so what is kibr?"" He said: ""Is it that one of us has two good sandals with two good straps?"" He said: ""No."" He said: ""Is it that one of us has companions who sit with him?"" He said: ""No."" It was said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Then what is kibr?"" He said: ""Rejecting the truth and despising people."""
"3131","[AI-translation] Jabir said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, used to deliver the sermon leaning against a palm trunk. A woman from the Ansar who had a carpenter slave said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I have a carpenter slave, shall I order him to make a pulpit for you to deliver the sermon upon?"" He said: ""Yes."" He said: So he made a pulpit for him. He said: When it was Friday, he delivered the sermon on the pulpit. He said: The trunk upon which he used to stand moaned as a child moans. The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""Verily, this wept for what it missed of the mention."
"3132","[AI-translation] Darda' said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""I am your share of the prophets, and you are my share of the nations."
"3133","[AI-translation] 'Ata' reported from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: ""We, the company of prophets, our eyes sleep but our hearts do not sleep."
"3134","On the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka'b, who said: Two men boasted of their lineage during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). One of them said: ""I am so-and-so, son of so-and-so. Who are you? May you have no mother!"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Two men boasted of their lineage during the time of Moses (peace be upon him). One of them said: 'I am so-and-so, son of so-and-so,' until he counted nine [ancestors]. 'Who are you? May you have no mother!' The other said: 'I am so-and-so, son of so-and-so, son of Islam.' Then Allah revealed to Moses (peace be upon him): 'Say to these two boasters: As for you who boast of nine ancestors, you are the tenth of them in the Fire. And as for you who boast of two ancestors, you are the third of them in Paradise.'"""
"3135","From Masruq, he said: I was reclining with ʿĀʾishah when she said: “O Abū ʿĀʾishah! Three things — whoever speaks one of them has fabricated a tremendous lie against Allah.” (I said: “What are they?” She said: “Whoever claims that Muḥammad (peace be upon him) saw his Lord has fabricated a tremendous lie against Allah.”) He said: I was reclining, so I sat up and said: “O Mother of the Believers! Give me time and do not rush me. Did not Allah, Mighty and Majestic, say: ‘And certainly he saw him in the clear horizon’ (Al‑Takwīr: 23) and ‘And certainly he saw him in another descent’ (Al‑Najm: 13)?” She said: “I am the first of this nation to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) about that, so he said: ‘It is only Gabriel; I did not see him in his true form in which he was created except these two times. I saw him descending from the heaven, his great creation filling the space between the heaven and the earth.’” She said: “Did you not hear that Allah says: ‘Vision perceives Him not, but He perceives all vision; and He is the Subtle, the Acquainted’ (Al‑Anʿām: 103)? Did you not hear that Allah says: ‘And it is not for any human being that Allah should speak to him except by revelation or from behind a partition or that He sends a messenger to reveal, by His permission, what He wills. Indeed, He is Most High and Wise’ (Al‑Shūrā: 51)?” She said: “And whoever claims that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) concealed something from the Book of Allah has fabricated a tremendous lie against Allah. And Allah says: ‘O Messenger, announce that which has been revealed to you from your Lord, and if you do not, then you have not conveyed His message’ (Al‑Māʾidah: 67).” She said: “And whoever claims that he informs about what will be tomorrow has fabricated a tremendous lie against Allah. And Allah says: ‘Say, “None in the heavens and earth knows the unseen except Allah”’ (Al‑Naml: 65).”"
"3136","[AI-translation] Aisha said: The Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, used to say while he was healthy: ""No prophet is taken until he sees his place in Paradise and then is given a choice."" When death approached him and his head was on my thigh, he lost consciousness, then he recovered and looked up to the ceiling of the house, then he said: ""O Allah! The Highest Companion."" I said: ""Then he will not choose us,"" and I knew that it was the hadith he used to narrate to us while he was healthy. She said: The last word he spoke was: ""O Allah! The Highest Companion."
"3137","[AI-translation] Ibn Abbas reported from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: ""Musa, peace be upon him, was given the Tablets, and I was given the Mathani."
"3138","[AI-translation] Anas reported that the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""The first prophet to be sent was Nuh."
"3139","[AI-translation] Anas said: The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""Which of creation is most amazing in faith?"" They said: ""The angels."" He said: ""The angels, how could they not believe?"" They said: ""The prophets."" He said: ""The prophets have revelation sent to them, so how could they not believe?"" They said: ""The Companions."" He said: ""The Companions are with the prophets, so how could they not believe? But the most amazing of people in faith are a people who will come after you and find a book of revelation and believe in it and follow it. They are the most amazing of people—or of creation—in faith."
"3140","On the authority of Abu Hurayrah, attributed to the Prophet: ""The prophets are brothers from different mothers; their mothers are different but their religion is one. And I am the closest of people to Jesus son of Mary, for there is no prophet between me and him. And he will descend. So when you see him, recognize him: a man of medium build, reddish-white, between two yellow garments, as if his head is dripping with water though no moisture has touched it. He will fight the people for Islam, break the cross, kill the pig, and abolish the jizya. And Allah will destroy in his time all religions except Islam. And Allah will destroy the False Messiah. And security will prevail on the earth until lions graze with camels, leopards with cattle, wolves with sheep, and children play with snakes without being harmed. He will remain on earth for forty years, then he will die, and the Muslims will pray over him."""
"3141","[AI-translation] Anas reported, elevating it to the Prophet: ""The prophets—may Allah's peace be upon them—are alive in their graves, praying."
"3142","[AI-translation] Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported, elevating it to the Prophet: ""I was sent from the best of the generations of the Children of Adam, generation after generation, until I was sent from the generation in which I was."
"3143","[AI-translation] Abu Hurairah reported from the Prophet, peace be upon him: ""While Ayyub was bathing naked, a swarm of gold locusts fell upon him, and Ayyub began to gather them in his garment. His Lord called out to him: 'O Ayyub! Did I not make you independent of what you see?' He said: 'Yes, by Your Might! But I have no independence from Your blessing.'"
"3144","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: ""Blessing is in the forelocks of horses."
"3145","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas, marfu': ""Al-Bayt al-Ma'mur is in the seventh heaven. A thousand angels enter it every day, then they do not return to it until the Hour is established."
"3146","[AI-translation] Narrated Tawus from Abu Hurayrah who said: ""Isa received his proof, so Allah met him in His saying: then the rest was raised."" Abu Hurayrah reported from the Prophet, peace be upon him: ""So Allah met him: the entire verse."
"3147","Ibn Abbas narrated: The Jews came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and said: ""O Abul-Qasim! We will ask you about some things; if you answer them for us, we will follow you, believe you, and have faith in you."" He said: So he took from them the covenant that Israel (Jacob) took upon himself. They said: ""Allah is Witness over what we say."" They said: ""Inform us about the sign of the Prophet (peace be upon him)."" He said: ""His eyes sleep, but his heart does not sleep."" They said: ""Inform us how a woman bears a female child and how she bears a male child."" He said: ""The two fluids meet; if the woman's fluid prevails over the man's fluid, it becomes female, and if the man's fluid prevails over the woman's fluid, it becomes male."" They said: ""You have spoken the truth."" They said: ""Then inform us about thunder, what is it?"" He said: ""Thunder is an angel from among the angels, appointed over the clouds; in his hand (or in his hands) is a whip of fire with which he drives the clouds. And the sound that is heard from him is his driving of the clouds when he drives them until they reach where he is commanded."""
"3148","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: ""My eyes sleep, but my heart does not sleep."
"3149","Jabir ibn Abdullah reported: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Narrate from the Children of Israel, and there is no harm in that; for there were wonders among them."" Then he began to narrate. He said: ""A group from the Children of Israel went out until they came to one of their graveyards. They said: 'Let us pray two rak'ahs and supplicate to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, that He brings out for us a man from those who have died, so we may ask him about death.' So they did that. While they were in that state, a man stuck his head out from one of those graves, with the mark of prostration between his eyes. He said: 'O people! What did you want from me? I have been dead for a hundred years, and the heat of death has not subsided from me until now. So supplicate to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, for me that He returns me as I was.'"""
"3150","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Abbas from the Prophet, peace be upon him, who said: ""Snakes are the transformation of the jinn, just as monkeys and pigs were transformed from the Children of Israel."
"3151","[AI-translation] Aishah reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""The snake is wicked, the scorpion is wicked, the mouse is wicked, and the crow is wicked."
"3152","[AI-translation] Darda', marfu': ""When Allah created Adam, He struck his right shoulder and brought forth a white offspring as if they were ants. Then He struck his left shoulder and brought forth a black offspring as if they were charcoal. He said to those on His right: 'To Paradise, and I do not care,' and He said to those in His left palm: 'To the Fire, and I do not care.'"
"3153","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurayrah, marfu': ""Allah created Adam in His image, his height being sixty cubits. When He created him, He said: 'Go and greet that group of angels who are sitting, and listen to what they greet you with, for it is your greeting and the greeting of your offspring.' So he said: 'As-salamu alaykum.' They said: 'As-salamu alayka wa rahmatullah.' They added to him 'wa rahmatullah.' Everyone who enters Paradise will be in the image of Adam. Since then, creation has continued to decrease until now."
"3154","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, took my hand and said: ""Allah, Mighty and Majestic, created the soil on Saturday, and created the mountains in it on Sunday, and created the trees on Monday, and created the disliked things on Tuesday, and created the light on Wednesday, and scattered the animals in it on Thursday, and created Adam, peace be upon him, after Asr on Friday, at the end of creation, in the last hour of the hours of Friday, between Asr and night."
"3155","[AI-translation] Narrated Aishah, marfu': ""The angels were created from light, Iblis was created from the fire of Samum, and Adam, peace be upon him, was created from what has been described to you."
"3156","[AI-translation] Madinah, so the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: He was buried in the clay from which he was created."
"3157","[AI-translation] From Anas bin Malik who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, and said: O best of creation! So the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: That is Ibrahim, peace be upon him."
"3158","[AI-translation] From Anas, raised to the Prophet: I saw, on the night I was taken on the Night Journey, a people whose lips were being cut with scissors of fire. I said: Who are these, O Jibril? He said: Preachers from your nation who enjoin goodness upon the people and forget themselves, while they read the Book. Do they not understand?"
"3159","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, raised to the Prophet: Sidrat al-Muntaha was raised for me in the seventh heaven. Its fruits were like the jars of Hajar, and its leaves were like the ears of elephants. From its base emerged two outward rivers and two inward rivers. I said: O Jibril, what are these? He said: As for the inward ones, they are in Paradise, and as for the outward ones, they are the Nile and the Euphrates."
"3160","[AI-translation] Khattab, raised to the Prophet: The wind is sent as a punishment for some people and as a mercy for others."
"3161","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: I asked Jibril, peace be upon him: ""Which of the two terms did Musa, peace be upon him, fulfill?"" He said: ""The more complete and perfect of the two."
"3162","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, raised to the Prophet: Sayhan, Jaihan, the Euphrates, and the Nile are all from the rivers of Paradise."
"3163","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, raised to the Prophet: I marvel at the patience of my brother Yusuf and his generosity, may Allah forgive him, when he was sent to so that he could be consulted about the dream; had it been me, I would not have done so until I left. And I marvel at his patience and his generosity, may Allah forgive him, when he was summoned to come out but he did not come out until he informed them of his excuse; had it been me, I would have rushed to the door. Were it not for that word, he would not have remained in prison, seeking relief from other than Allah, His saying: ""Mention me to your master"" [Yusuf: 42]."
"3164","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, raised to the Prophet: Four rivers were made to gush forth from Paradise: the Euphrates, the Nile, Sayhan, and Jaihan."
"3165","[AI-translation] From Anas bin Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said to Jibril, peace be upon him: Why is it that I have never seen Mika'il laughing? He said: Mika'il has not laughed since the Fire was created."
"3166","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah, raised to the Prophet: The first to host a guest was Ibrahim, and he was the first to be circumcised at the age of eighty years, and he circumcised himself with a Qadum."
"3167","[AI-translation] Darda' who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Dawud was the most devout of mankind."
"3168","Urwah reported: Aisha said: ""O son of my sister! The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) did not prefer any of us over another in the division of his time spent with us. Scarcely a day passed without him visiting all of us, drawing near to each woman without touching her until he reached the one whose turn it was, and he would spend the night with her. And Sawdah bint Zam'ah, when she grew old and feared that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) might separate from her, said: 'O Messenger of Allah! My day is for Aisha.' So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) accepted that from her. And concerning this, Allah the Exalted revealed [the verse], and in similar cases, I think he said: 'And if a woman fears from her husband ill-treatment or desertion...' (An-Nisa: 128)."
"3169","[AI-translation] Khudri that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: There was a short woman among the Children of Israel who made two legs of wood and walked between two short women. She made a gold ring and placed the finest musk perfume under its stone. When she passed by a gathering, she would move it and its fragrance would waft. In another narration: She made a clasp for it, and when she passed by the gathering, she would touch it and it would open, and its fragrance would emanate."
"3170","[AI-translation] Narrated Jundub bin 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Among those before you was a man who had a wound. He became impatient, took a knife, and cut his hand with it. The blood did not stop until he died. Allah, the Exalted, said: My servant hastened his soul; I have forbidden Paradise to him."
"3171","[AI-translation] Narrated Dhu Makhbar, raised to the Prophet: This matter was in Himyar, so Allah removed it from them and made it in Quraysh."
"3172","ʿUtbah ibn ʿAbd al-Sulamī narrated to them—and he was one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: A man asked him, ""How was your early life, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""My wet-nurse was from Banū Saʿd ibn Bakr. I went out with a son of hers to our herd of camels, and we had not taken any provisions with us. I said: 'O my brother! Go and bring us some provisions from our mother.' So my brother went off, and I stayed with the herd. Then two white birds, as if they were two eagles, came flying toward me. One of them said to the other: 'Is it he?' The other said: 'Yes.' They came rushing at me, seized me, threw me down on my back, split open my belly, then extracted my heart, split it open, and removed from it two black clots. One of them said to the other: 'Bring me water of snow.' So he washed my interior with it. Then he said: 'Bring me water of hail.' So he washed my heart with it. Then he said: 'Bring me the Sakīnah (tranquility).' So he cast it into my heart. Then one of them said to the other: 'Seal it.' So he sealed it and stamped it with the Seal of Prophethood. Then one of them said to the other: 'Put him in one scale, and put a thousand of his Ummah in the other scale.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Then I saw the thousand above me, and I feared that some of them might fall upon me.' He said: 'If his Ummah were weighed against him, he would outweigh them.' Then they departed and left me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I was seized with a severe fright. Then I went to my mother and informed her of what I had encountered. She feared that something might have befallen me, so she said: ""I seek refuge for you with Allah."" She saddled a camel of hers, placed me on the saddle, and rode behind me until we reached my mother (i.e., his wet-nurse). She said: ""Have I fulfilled my trust and my covenant?"" And she told her what I had encountered. That did not alarm her, and she said: ""I saw a light emerge from me—meaning—illuminating the palaces of Shām."""
"3173","[AI-translation] Narrated 'Abdullah, raised to the Prophet: It is as if I am looking at Musa, peace be upon him, in this valley in a state of Ihram, wearing two Qutwaniyyah garments."
"3174","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""It is as if I am looking at Musa bin 'Imran descending from Thaniyyat Harsha, walking."
"3175","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: Every son of Adam has his share of Zina; there is no escaping it. The Zina of the eye is looking, the Zina of the hand is touching, the soul desires and whispers, and the private parts confirm or deny it."
"3176","[AI-translation] Narrated 'Aishah who said: Umm Bishr bint al-Bara' bin Ma'rur entered upon the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, during the illness in which he died while he had a fever, and she touched him. She said: I have not seen a fever like yours upon anyone. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: As our reward is multiplied, so is our trial multiplied."
"3177","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Dharr who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Allah did not send any prophet except in the language of his people."
"3178","[AI-translation] Marfu' from Anas: When Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, fashioned Adam, peace be upon him, He left him, so Iblis started circumambulating him, looking at him. When he saw he was hollow, he said: I have overtaken him, a creation that cannot restrain itself."
"3179","[AI-translation] Narrated from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, that the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""When Musa met Khidr, peace be upon them both, a bird came and dipped its beak in the water. Khidr said to Musa: Do you know what this bird is saying? He said: What is it saying? He said: It is saying: Your knowledge and the knowledge of Musa in the knowledge of Allah is but like what my beak has taken from the water."
"3180","[AI-translation] Marfu' from Anas: When Allah blew the soul into Adam, and the soul reached his head, he sneezed and said: Praise be to Allah, the Lord of the Worlds. He, Blessed and Exalted is He, said to him: May Allah have mercy upon you."
"3181","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""If Allah were to punish me and 'Isa for our sins (in a narration: for what these two have committed, meaning the thumb and the one next to it), He would punish us and not (in another: and would not) wrong us in the least."
"3182","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: If I had remained in prison as long as Yusuf remained, then the caller came to me, I would have answered him, whereas when the messenger came to him, he said: ""Return to your lord and ask him what is the matter with the women who cut their hands. Indeed, my lord is knowing of their plot"" (50). And may Allah have mercy on Lut. Indeed, he used to seek refuge in a strong support, when he said to his people: ""If only I had power against you, or could take refuge in a strong support"" (80). And Allah did not send after him any prophet except among the wealthy of his people."
"3183","[AI-translation] Narrated from Ibn 'Abbas and from Anas, who both said: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) used to deliver the khutbah leaning against a trunk. When the minbar was made, he went to the minbar, and the trunk yearned. He went to it and embraced it, and it calmed down. He said: If I had not embraced it, it would have yearned until the Day of Resurrection."
"3184","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Umamah that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say: A people will surely enter Paradise by the intercession of a man who is not a prophet, like the two tribes or like one of the two tribes of Rabi'ah and Mudar. A man said: O Messenger of Allah! What is Rabi'ah of Mudar? He said: I only say what I am told."
"3185","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: I do not know whether Tubba' was accursed or not, and I do not know whether Dhul-Qarnayn was a prophet or not, and I do not know whether the prescribed punishments are expiations or not."
"3186","[AI-translation] Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him): ""And Allah has not destroyed any people, generation, nation, or inhabitants of a town since He sent down the Torah upon the earth with a punishment from the sky, except the people of the village that were turned into apes. Have you not seen the statement of the Exalted: 'And We gave Musa the Scripture after We had destroyed the former generations, as enlightenment for the people and guidance and mercy that they might be reminded' (43) (Al-Qasas)."
"3187","[AI-translation] Sulami (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family), who said: ""The sun does not rise without anything of Allah's creation, Mighty and Majestic is He, glorifying Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, and praising Him, except what is of the Shaytan and the most arrogant of the children of Adam."" He was asked about the most arrogant of the children of Adam, and he said: ""The worst of creation"" - or he said: ""The worst of the creation of Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He."
"3188","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah (marfu'an): The sun was never held back for any human being except for Yusha' bin Nun during the nights he journeyed to Bait al-Maqdis."
"3189","[AI-translation] Ghifari, who said: I entered the Masjid al-Haram, and I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, sitting alone, so I sat beside him and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Which verse revealed to you is the greatest?"" He said: ""Ayat al-Kursi. The seven heavens compared to the Kursi are nothing but like a ring thrown into a barren land, and the superiority of the Throne over the Kursi is like the superiority of that barren land over that ring."
"3190","[AI-translation] Qurashi: That the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, spat one day onto his palm, placed his finger on it, and then said: ""Allah, the Exalted, says: O son of Adam! How can you overpower Me when I created you from something like this, until when I fashioned you and proportioned you, you walked between two garments, and the earth had from you a heavy burden? So you amassed and withheld, until when your soul reached this"" — and he pointed to his throat — ""(and in a narration: until it reached the collarbones) you said: 'I give in charity,' but how is it the time for giving in charity?"
"3191","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Abbas (marfu'an): I did not pass by any assembly of angels on the night I was taken on the Night Journey except that each of them said to me: ""O Muhammad, adhere to cupping (hijamah)."
"3192","[AI-translation] Narrated Abdullah bin Umar (marfu'an): No nation has ever been metamorphosed and then left offspring."
"3193","[AI-translation] He, peace be upon him, said: There is no one from the offspring of Adam except that he has erred or intended to commit a sin, except Yahya bin Zakariya. It was narrated from Abdullah bin Abbas, Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, from his father Amr, Abu Hurairah, and Al-Hasan Al-Basri as mursal, and Yahya bin Ba'dah as mursal."
"3194","[AI-translation] Khuza'i, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, mounted us on weak camels from the charity camels for Hajj. We said: ""O Messenger of Allah! How do you expect these to carry us?"" He said: ""There is no camel except that on its hump is a shaytan. So mention the name of Allah when you ride them as He commanded you, then make them subservient for yourselves, for it is Allah who carries."
"3195","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Abbas, who said: ""There is no year that has more rain than any other year, but Allah distributes it among His creation (wherever He wills)."" Then he recited: ""And We have distributed it among them, that they may remember"" [Al-Furqan: 50]."
"3196","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: I was sitting with the Prophet (peace be upon him) when a funeral procession passed by. He asked: ""What is this?"" They said: ""The funeral of so-and-so, who used to love Allah and His Messenger, act in obedience to Allah, and strive in it."" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""It is confirmed, it is confirmed, it is confirmed."" Then another funeral procession passed by, and they said: ""The funeral of so-and-so, who used to hate Allah and His Messenger, act in disobedience to Allah, and strive in it."" He said: ""It is confirmed, it is confirmed, it is confirmed."" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Your statement regarding the funeral, and your praise of it — you praised the first with good, and the last with evil, yet you said regarding both: 'It is confirmed, it is confirmed, it is confirmed.'"" He said: ""Yes, O Abu Bakr! Indeed Allah has angels who speak on the tongues of the children of Adam regarding the good and evil that is in a person."""
"3197","[AI-translation] Narrated Jabir (marfu'an): I passed by Jibril on the night I was taken on the Night Journey at the Highest Assembly, and he was like a worn-out garment out of the fear of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"3198","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""On the night I was taken on the Night Journey, I passed by Musa and saw him standing, praying in his grave (at the red sand dune)."
"3199","[AI-translation] From Abu Juhayfah from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, who said: ""Whoever sees me in a dream, it is as if he has seen me in a waking state, for Satan cannot take my form."
"3200","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet: ""Whoever is pleased to look at the humility of Isa, let him look at Abu Dharr."
"3201","[AI-translation] From Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""Musa ibn Imran is the chosen one of Allah."
"3202","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: ""The Black Stone descended from Paradise, and it was whiter than snow, but the sins of the children of Adam blackened it."
"3203","[AI-translation] From Abu Umamah, that a man said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Was Adam a prophet?"" He said: ""Yes, a taught one, spoken to."" He said: ""How much was between him and Nuh?"" He said: ""Ten centuries."" He said: ""How much was between Nuh and Ibrahim?"" He said: ""Ten centuries."" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah! How many were the messengers?"" He said: ""Three hundred and fifteen, a large throng."
"3204","[AI-translation] From Abu Umamah, that a man said: ""O Messenger of Allah, was Adam a prophet?"" He said: ""Yes, spoken to."" He said: ""How much was between him and Nuh?"" He said: ""Ten centuries."" He said: ""O Messenger of Allah! How many were the messengers?"" He said: ""Three hundred and fifteen."
"3205","[AI-translation] From Abu Dharr who said: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, on a donkey while the sun was at its setting, and he said: ""Do you know where this sets?"" I said: ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" He said: ""It sets in a hot spring, then it goes until it falls down before its Lord, Mighty and Majestic, prostrating beneath the Throne. And when it is time for it to emerge, Allah gives it permission to emerge, and it rises. And when He intends to make it rise from where it sets, He holds it back, so it says: 'O my Lord! My journey is far.' So He says to it: 'Rise from where you set.' That is when (no soul will benefit from its faith)."
"3206","[AI-translation] From Hakim ibn Hizam, who said: While the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, was with his companions, he said to them: ""Do you hear what I hear?"" They said: ""We do not hear anything."" He said: ""I can hear the creaking of the heaven, and it is not blamed for creaking, for there is no spot in it the size of a hand span except that there is an angel upon it, either prostrating or standing."
"3207","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah who said: Jibril sat with the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, and looked at the sky, and there was an angel descending. Jibril said to him: ""This angel has not descended since the day he was created before the Hour."" When he descended, he said: ""O Muhammad! Your Lord has sent me to you: 'Shall I make you a king or a servant-messenger?'"" Jibril said to him: ""Be humble to your Lord, O Muhammad!"" So the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""No, rather a servant-messenger."
"3208","[AI-translation] The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Do not insult Tubba, for he had embraced Islam."" Narrated from the hadith of........"
"3209","[AI-translation] Numayri, raised [to the Prophet]: ""Do not kill the locusts, for it is one of the greatest armies of Allah."
"3210","On the authority of Abu Dharr al-Ghifari, who said: I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! How did you know that you are a Prophet until you became certain?"" He said: ""O Abu Dharr, two angels came to me while I was in some of the valleys of Mecca. One of them descended to the earth, and the other was between the heaven and the earth. One of them said to his companion: 'Is it him?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then weigh him against a man.' So I was weighed against him, and I outweighed him. Then he said: 'Weigh him against ten.' So I was weighed against them, and I outweighed them. Then he said: 'Weigh him against a hundred.' So I was weighed against them, and I outweighed them. Then he said: 'Weigh him against a thousand.' So I was weighed against them, and I outweighed them, as if I see them scattering over me due to the lightness of the scale. Then one of them said to his companion: 'If you had weighed him against his Ummah, he would have outweighed it.'"""
"3211","[AI-translation] From A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""There is no space in the lowest heaven the size of a foot except that upon it is an angel, prostrating or standing. That is the saying of the angels: 'And there is not among us but has a known position. And indeed, we are those who line up in rows. And indeed, we are those who exalt [Allah].' (As-Saffat)."
